    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick for side sleepers with sore hips who want deep cushioning without losing support at the waist.",
    "description": "Side sleepers with hip pain usually want more cushion than a medium bed gives, and the risk with a soft mattress is that the waist sinks along with the hip. The Evolution 15 in Plush is our answer to that problem. Nolah makes it in three firmnesses, and the Plush is the softest mattress on this list, with reviewers placing it around 5 out of 10. What keeps it from turning into a hammock is the support system underneath. The Amazon listing describes HDMax Tri-Zone coils divided into three support zones, including a lumbar region, over 8-inch individually wrapped coils with reinforced perimeter coils. So the hip has a thick comfort layer to sink into, a Euro topper and graphite-infused foam that Nolah markets for cooling, while the middle of the bed still pushes back. Many side sleepers with hip pain prefer this kind of bed: soft on top, zoned underneath. The trade-offs are price and size. It is a premium hybrid, it stands 15 inches tall, and some reviewers found the edges softer than they expected. If you share the bed with a back or stomach sleeper, the Luxury Firm version is a compromise that still suits lighter side sleepers. If your budget is lower, the Brooklyn Bedding Signature Hybrid in Soft is the closest value alternative."
  },
  {
    "id": "brooklyn-bedding-signature-hybrid",
    "name": "Brooklyn Bedding Signature Hybrid Mattress",
    "category": "13.25-Inch Hybrid, Soft / Medium / Firm, Optional Pillow Top",
    "badge": "Best Value Hybrid",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
