          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best mattress for side sleepers with hip pain?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Many side sleepers with hip pain prefer a plush hybrid or a mattress with a thick Euro top, such as the Nolah Evolution 15 in Plush. The soft top lets the hip sink while coils keep the waist supported. A pillow between the knees helps too. Talk to a doctor or physical therapist about pain that persists."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best mattress for side sleepers with back pain?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Side sleepers with back pain usually need zoned support, which makes the middle of the bed firmer than the shoulder area so the waist does not sag. The Helix Midnight Luxe is built that way. A medium feel, around 6 out of 10, is a good starting point for most average-weight side sleepers."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is memory foam or hybrid better for side sleepers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Both work. Memory foam contours closely and isolates motion, which suits side sleepers who lie still and sleep cool. Hybrids add coils for waist support, airflow and easier movement, which suits heavier side sleepers, combination sleepers and hot sleepers. If you are unsure which suits you, a medium hybrid is the safer first choice."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why do my shoulders hurt when I sleep on my side?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Shoulder pain on waking often means the mattress is too firm for side sleeping, so the shoulder cannot sink and takes pressure all night. A pillow that is too low can add to it. A softer mattress or a 2 to 3 inch topper may help; persistent shoulder pain is worth checking with a doctor."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a topper make a firm mattress good for side sleeping?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Often, yes. If your mattress is flat and supportive but too firm, a 2 to 3 inch memory foam or latex topper can add the shoulder and hip cushioning a side sleeper needs. A topper cannot fix a mattress that sags in the middle, which needs replacing instead, because the topper simply follows the dip."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
