          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Side sleepers need soft where the body is wide and support where it is narrow. For most people that means a medium hybrid with a cushioned top and, ideally, zoned support: the Helix Midnight Luxe does it best. The Purple Plus suits sharp shoulder pressure and hot sleepers, the Nolah Evolution 15 in Plush suits sore hips, and the Brooklyn Bedding Signature Hybrid and Zinus Green Tea cover tighter budgets.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose firmness for your weight, pair the bed with the right pillow, and give it a month before you judge it. If shoulder, hip or back pain persists, talk to your doctor or physical therapist.
